## How the drag was verified

The cached headless Chromium has no test-runner input driver, so the interaction was verified with a
temporary same-origin probe page (an iframe of the real preview at 1440 × 900 and at 390 × 844) that
dispatched real `PointerEvent` / `KeyboardEvent` sequences into the page; the preview's own listeners
handled them exactly as for real input. `setPointerCapture` is best-effort in `preview.js`, so
synthetic pointer ids do not break the drag. The probe file was removed before the commit and is not
part of the deliverable. Results:

```
desktop start a={"x":32,"y":16} b={"x":864,"y":208}
desktop clickUnder4px moved=false
desktop arrowRight16=true arrowDown16=true
desktop homeReset=true
desktop dragMoved=true otherCardFixed=true edgeFollowed=true
desktop selected=true dragClassCleared=true
desktop clampInside=true
desktop overflow=false scrollWidth=1440 clientWidth=1440
mobile overflow=false scrollWidth=390 clientWidth=390 cardsInside=true surface=358x360
```

Pointer and keyboard logic, manually described:

- `pointerdown` on a whole card selects it (1.5 px `--accent` border + `--accent-soft` ring) and calls
  `setPointerCapture`; movement starts only after the 4 px `--drag-threshold`, so a click with a 2 px
  wobble selects but does not move (verified: `clickUnder4px moved=false`).
- During the drag the card position is clamped to the dot-grid surface and the SVG edge is redrawn on
  every move from the two card rectangles (nearest horizontal sides, vertical sides, corners, or the
  nearest overlapping side pair). The edge uses `--layer-edges`, the cards `--layer-note-cards`, so
  the edge stays below the cards. An 80/48 px drag moved card A, left card B in place and changed the
  edge endpoints (verified: `dragMoved=true otherCardFixed=true edgeFollowed=true`); a 5000 px drag
  clamped the card inside the surface (`clampInside=true`).
- `pointerup` / `pointercancel` end the drag, remove the `is-dragging` state and announce the grid
  position in the `aria-live` status.
- Keyboard: each card is focused with a visible `--accent` focus outline; arrow keys move by one
  canvas grid step (`--canvas-grid`, 16 px), `Home` returns both cards to their start positions; the
  handled keys call `preventDefault` so the page does not scroll (verified: `arrowRight16=true`,
  `arrowDown16=true`, `homeReset=true`).
- `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` disables the remaining transitions (global rule in `preview.css`).
- Both viewports have no horizontal overflow (1440/1440 and 390/390); the mobile cards stay inside
  the 358 × 360 demo surface. The P0-19 static sections are unchanged below the new demo section.

